  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
<para>What information does a correlation coefficient tell you about the data in a scatter plot?  
</para>
</problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
    <para>The sign of the correlation coefficient matches the sign of the slope for the best fit line. The closer the correlation coefficient value is to 0, the weaker the linear relationship. The closer the correlation coefficient is to 1 or –1, the stronger the linear relationship.
      </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
<para>Which value best estimates the value for the correlation coefficient of the scatter plot: –1, –0.8, –0.2, 0.2, 0.8, or 1? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
<figure><media alt="Graph of a scatter plot, xy-plane, origin O."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a194323f9d13066c9d3dca668e5c259c8c226c7a"/></media></figure></problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
    <para>–0.8, since the points form a fairly strong linear pattern that is decreasing to the right</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
